WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:06.523
Once upon a time, a sly fox lived in a forest.

2
00:00:06.524 --> 00:00:12.578
In that same forest, there lived an annoying crow.

3
00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:16.663
Crow loved to brag about herself.

4
00:00:16.664 --> 00:00:25.963
She thought she was the best creature in the forest.

5
00:00:25.964 --> 00:00:32.375
Every morning she sang loudly, waking up all the animals.

6
00:00:32.376 --> 00:00:39.360
Crow thought she sang beautifully, but she was not a good singer.

7
00:00:39.361 --> 00:00:45.949
Fox especially hated her singing.

8
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:50.720
One morning Fox was sleeping under a tree.

9
00:00:50.721 --> 00:00:54.888
Crow's noisy song woke him up as usual.

10
00:00:54.889 --> 00:00:59.209
He was about to scold Crow when she flew away.

11
00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:11.930
"Grr," Fox thought. "I need to teach Crow a lesson!"

12
00:01:11.931 --> 00:01:15.055
Fox went back to sleep.

13
00:01:15.056 --> 00:01:18.900
Soon a flapping noise woke him up again.

14
00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:23.160
Fox looked up and saw Crow returning.

15
00:01:23.161 --> 00:01:27.805
In her beak she was holding a big piece of cheese.

16
00:01:27.806 --> 00:01:31.693
Fox's stomach growled.

17
00:01:31.694 --> 00:01:35.417
"I'm hungry," he thought.

18
00:01:35.418 --> 00:01:38.686
"And that cheese looks delicious.

19
00:01:38.687 --> 00:01:42.688
But Crow will never share that cheese with me."

20
00:01:42.689 --> 00:01:45.501
He watched Crow for a moment.

21
00:01:45.502 --> 00:01:52.421
She was flapping her wings again to show them off.

22
00:01:52.422 --> 00:01:57.403
"I know what to do," Fox thought.

23
00:01:57.404 --> 00:02:00.024
He stood up and stretched.

24
00:02:00.025 --> 00:02:05.217
"Ahh." He yawned loudly.

25
00:02:05.218 --> 00:02:10.040
Then he pretended to suddenly spot Crow.

26
00:02:10.041 --> 00:02:14.059
"Oh! Good morning, Crow," he said.

27
00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:18.451
Crow ignored him and kept showing off her wings.

28
00:02:18.452 --> 00:02:22.511
Fox pretended to stare at her feathers.

29
00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:27.315
Then he put his paw on his heart.

30
00:02:27.316 --> 00:02:30.972
"Am I still dreaming?" he cried.

31
00:02:30.973 --> 00:02:36.750
"Why, Crow, I never noticed how beautiful your feathers are!"

32
00:02:36.751 --> 00:02:39.815
Crow spread her wings wider.

33
00:02:39.816 --> 00:02:42.912
She raised her beak high.

34
00:02:42.913 --> 00:02:46.259
Fox watched the piece of cheese.

35
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.985
He licked his lips, but Crow didn't notice.

36
00:02:50.986 --> 00:02:56.410
"I mean, just look at your feathers!" Fox went on.

37
00:02:56.411 --> 00:03:00.029
"They shine like the sun!"

38
00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.181
Finally Crow looked down at Fox.

39
00:03:04.182 --> 00:03:10.090
As soon as she did, Fox let out a loud gasp.

40
00:03:10.091 --> 00:03:16.377
"And your eyes! They glow like the moon!"

41
00:03:16.378 --> 00:03:22.214
Crow nodded. The cheese stayed firmly in her beak.

42
00:03:22.215 --> 00:03:25.469
Fox looked at Crow slyly.

43
00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.319
"But I think your voice is the most beautiful thing of all.

44
00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:33.638
I love hearing your song every morning!

45
00:03:33.639 --> 00:03:37.742
Would you sing something for me now?"

46
00:03:37.743 --> 00:03:42.073
Fox's compliments filled Crow with delight.

47
00:03:42.074 --> 00:03:45.747
She stood tall and got ready to sing.

48
00:03:45.748 --> 00:03:50.584
She opened her beak . . . and down fell the cheese.

49
00:03:50.585 --> 00:03:53.323
Fox leaped to catch the treat.

50
00:03:53.324 --> 00:03:57.156
Then he gobbled it down.

51
00:03:57.157 --> 00:04:00.165
Crow watched in horror.

52
00:04:00.166 --> 00:04:04.794
"My cheese! You tricked me, Fox!"

53
00:04:04.795 --> 00:04:07.265
Fox grinned.

54
00:04:07.266 --> 00:04:12.628
"Your feathers are pretty, but let me give you some advice.

55
00:04:12.629 --> 00:04:20.884
Don't trust those who flatter you!"

